Subject: [PATCH] AROS host: DeckCraft in an Intuition window through egui-aros

apps/deckcraft-aros runs the egui interface with egui-aros: winit and egui-winit for the window and input, the CPU renderer or OpenGL chosen at run time (--gui-renderer, ToolType GUI_RENDERER, the GUI_RENDERER variable; AUTO by default), ASL requesters, the system clipboard for text and pictures (pictures handed to Paste as PNG). It follows the desktop app's start-up: preferences, AutoRecover, the sample, document names from the Shell or Workbench resolved by DOS, a .ppsx given last starts its show. Settings, the log and AutoRecover data live in DeckCraftData beside the program (DECKCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR); recent files kept by the 0.8.0 port as DOS names are converted when read. The program runs in the -nix path mode; requesters' DOS names are converted at the edge. --screenshot and --test-steps are test aids. The Cargo.lock entries for egui-aros come from the build (scripts/craft.py), as for the other Craft ports.
